ds with usbc are much faster than  lightning which is limited to usb 2.0  speeds and as far as legal troubles both  the biden harris administration and the  european union are pushing for usb-c  ports on all devices and in terms of the  environment apple could switch to usb-c  while at the same time removing the  cable from the box to help save the  environment and obviously save apple  cache so with that said we already have  leaks pointing to apple switching to  usb-c on the iphone 14 pro but i've got  even better evidence for why this makes  so much sense but first we've got to  take a look at all the three major  reasons for why apple gave the usbc port  to the ipad pro back in 2018. before  that point people were complaining about  the lightning port for years saying that  it was single handedly holding the ipad  pro back from being a true pro device  and as for the second reason usb-c was  required for some of the features that  apple was planning to give the ipad pro  like connecting fast external ssds to  help with professional editing as well  as connecting to external monitors which  is a feature that is not supported by  lightning and apple even showed off the  usbc port being used for various things  like connecting digital cameras for easy  file transfers charging an iphone  connecting to an audio mixer and once  again to a display and the third and  final reason for adding usbc was that  apple knew that they wanted to up the  base price of the ipad pro up to 799  dollars and there's no way that they  could have gotten away with it without  adding usbc to solve all of those  limitations and complaints and if you  really think about it every time apple  added usb-c to an ipad it came with a  price increase like the ipad air 4 in  2020 which got a hundred dollars more  expensive as well as the ipad mini 6  last year also a hundred dollars more  and part of that price increase was to  help compensate for lost revenues from  apple's lightning port because if you  didn't already know apple makes royalty  fees from every accessory out there that  uses a lightning port through their mfi  program so with that said before i  explain why it makes so much sense for  apple to switch to usbc on the iphone 14  pro models let me break down how i think  apple plans to make this usbc switch  happen to start i believe that apple is  planning on raising the base price of  the iphone 14 pro models because i don't  know if you remember or not but before  apple revealed the iphone 13 lineup it  was rumored that they would raise iphone  prices because their main chip supplier  tsmc  increased the pricing on their silicon  chip wafers and since we didn't get an  iphone price increase last year i  believe that it's coming this year  specifically with the iphone 14 pro  models getting a hundred dollars more  expensive however the problem is that  apple needs to justify the price  increase and the way that they've always  done this is with a full redesign which  for the upcoming iphone 14 has been  rumored for months now including the new  pill shaped cutout to replace the notch  on only the pro models as you can see in  this render that i had created by  shailesh so with that said many people  will gladly pay an extra hundred dollars  for that new hole punch display design  that looks very fresh but on the other  hand there are some people who could  care less about the notch since they've  gotten used to it over the past couple  of years and to them spending the extra  cash isn't worth it so apple would need  something else to entice people into  accepting the base price increase and i  fully believe that it could be the  switch to usbc because if you think  about it people have been asking for  usb-c for years now and apple has been  holding off for so long that if apple  made the switch right now then the  majority of consumers would be totally  shocked and blown away by this move by  apple and by doing this it could  single-handedly get people who  previously hated on apple for years to  finally soften up a bit and even  consider switching from an android to  the iphone and that's not even  mentioning the millions of people with  older iphones who will finally have a  great reason to upgrade to the 14 pro  just because of that usbc port that will  make their life so much easier if they  already have a bunch of other usbc  cables lying around so even if switching  to usbc would mean lost revenue for  apple from their lightning ecosystem the  vast number of new iphone sales because  of that new usb-c port would more than  make up for the lost revenue and if you  don't know what i mean by lost revenue  apple's lightning port is part of the  mfi program which means that every time  any company out there creates an  accessory like a lightning cable or  adapter apple charges a licensing  royalty for that lightning connector  bringing in a bunch of extra revenue and  that right there is probably why apple  has stuck to lightning for so long  because if they suddenly ditched it they  would lose out on all of that mfi  royalty revenue within a couple of years  but thankfully apple has been working on  the absolute perfect solution to this  problem which will make it much easier  to ditch lightning and that is of course  apple's new magsafe ecosystem for the  iphone if you didn't already know both  the mac safe case module and the maxsafe  charger module are also part of the mfi  program which means that apple makes  money for every single mac safe  accessory sold regardless of whether it  supports charging or not so max save is  already replacing the mfi profits from  apple's lightning connector and in my  opinion it's going to make much more  money than lightning since magsafe is  modern and it's many times more useful  in fact we've already made three videos  on useful mac safe accessories and my  absolute favorite iphone accessory i've  ever purchased in my life is this  magsafe vent mount charger for my car  which is incredibly convenient but  having max life in the mfi program is  absolutely genius for apple because it  has nothing to do with the wired  charging port since it's on the back of  the iphone so apple can easily switch to  usbc and still make a ton of revenue  from max safe mfi royalty fees so the  point that i'm trying to make is that  apple isn't going to ditch lightning  until they successfully create an  alternative ecosystem that will bring in  extra mfi royalty revenue from their  iphone and i fully believe that apple  has already achieved that goal with the  new max safe ecosystem and they're now  finally ready to begin ditching the  lightning port and making my point even  more convincing apple has recently added  magsafe charging support to both their  new airpods 3 and airpods pro cases and  even better the most reliable leaker out  there mark german believes that apple is  adding wireless magsafe support to the  ipad pro later this year to further push  the magsafe ecosystem forward and to  make it even crazier mark mentioned that  apple plans on giving the apple watch  magnetic max safe charger support as  well so if all of this comes to light it  proves that apple is going to be fully  invested in making max safe the new mfi  money maker to replace the old lightning  standard but now with all that said i  have one last reason for apple adding  usbc to the iphone 14 pro and i think  that this one is the final nail in the  coffin when apple finally added usb-c to  the ipad pro the main reason was that  lightning was severely limiting what the  ipad could do and i fully believe that  we've finally reached that point with  the iphone's lightning port with the  iphone 13 pro you can now record prores  video which takes up a massive amount of  storage space specifically six gigabytes  per minute for 4k prores  but the problem is that the lightning  port still only supports usb 2 speeds  meaning that transferring those prores  files takes forever for example michael  tobin on youtube did a prores first look  video and he said that it took between  one to one and a half hours to transfer  160 gigs of 4k prores video which  translates to only around 26 minutes of  footage and because of that super slow  lightning port transfer speed he said  that it's probably gonna discourage  users from recording in prores at all  but wait it gets even worse because  we've been recently getting some very  solid leaks and rumors from analysts  like mingchequo that point to the iphone  14 pro coming with a brand new 48  megapixel main camera that can shoot 8k  video yes i said 8k and i believe it's  gonna work using the same prores format  since apple is building prores encoders  and decoders into both their iphone and  mac chips to make shooting editing and  playing back prores footage use much  less power and this finally brings me to  a tweet from mkbhd on twitter mentioning  that ak prores video would use 24  gigabytes of storage space per minute so  yes the quality is gonna be insane but  if apple sticks to the lightning port on  the iphone 14 pro it'll literally take  over an hour to transfer only around six  minutes of 8k prores footage which is  completely unacceptable and unrealistic  and based on that final point along with  everything that i already mentioned in  this video including the leaks and  rumors i believe that there's a pretty  good chance that we will finally see the  usbc ports on the upcoming iphone 14 pro  and if you totally disagree with me go  ahead and comment your thoughts down  below but if you enjoyed this video  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one and definitely  check out one of those two right over  there thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]

